All non-source files in this directory (package.json, package-lock.json,
tsconfig.json, .vscodeignore, etc.) are governed by the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE at repo root).

Source files (.ts) in this directory and its subdirectories carry
SPDX-License-Identifier headers individually and are likewise Apache 2.0.

The VS Code extension is positioned as a customer-installable client
integration (mirrors the SDK's permissive license posture) so that
customers can fork it for internal use, contribute upstream, and so the
extension can be published to the VS Code Marketplace with a credible
open-source story.

This LICENSE file exists because JSON / TOML / lock files have no
standardized comment syntax for SPDX-License-Identifier headers.
license-check.yml reads this file's SPDX line as the directory-level
declaration.

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
